Memory is the complement of code.
Memory needs to be accurate and can be empty; it is better to have nothing than to have something inaccurate.
The key points of memory are: 1. What it is. 2. Why it happened. 3. When it occurred.
Long-term memory needs an expiration warning to prompt the model that the memory might be inaccurate.
Things that can be directly obtained from the code or tools should not be stored in memory.
